    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0520" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg422"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Swenson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 95.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 160, of March 29 last, reporting the action of the Danish
                    Government in banishing two American citizens from Denmark on the ground that
                    they are Mormon missionaries.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform you that the Department fully approves your course in
                    regard to the matter and has nothing to add to its instruction to Mr. Risley of
                    July 23, 1897 (<ref target="frus:frus1897/pg_123">Foreign Relations 1897, p.
                        123</ref>), which shows the present attitude of this Government toward
                    Mormon missionaries.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
